WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.752
Let’s build a customer record as a dictionary.

00:00:02.752 --> 00:00:07.662
The keys are id, visits, total_spent, and status.

00:00:07.662 --> 00:00:10.462
Each key points to one value.

00:00:10.462 --> 00:00:16.743
Instead of remembering positions, we can ask directly for customer id or customer visits.

00:00:17.469 --> 00:00:19.666
That makes the code much more readable.

00:00:19.666 --> 00:00:25.551
Customer bracket id clearly means “give me the customer ID.”

00:00:25.551 --> 00:00:30.779
Try adding another key such as region or membership level and print it.
